We consider the $\ell_2$-regularized least squares problem \[ \minimize{x\in\Real^p} \quad g(x) \defd  rac{\lambda}{2}
orm{x}^2 +  rac{1}{2n}\sum_{i=1}^n(a_i^Tx - b_i)^2, \] where to apply SG methods and SAG we can use \[ f_i(x) :=  rac{\lambda}{2}
orm{x}^2 +  rac{1}{2}(a_i^Tx - b_i)^2. \] If we use $b$ to denote a vector containing the values $b_i$ and $A$ to denote a matrix withs rows $a_i$, we can re-write this problem as \[ \minimize{x\in\Real^p} \quad  rac{\lambda}{2}
orm{x}^2 +  rac{1}{2n}
orm{Ax - b}^2. \]
